    "section": "31.6",
    "heading": "Modifying an item",
    "lineStart": 2503,
    "lineEnd": 2511
  },
  "section": "31.6",
  "rulesText": "Adding a feature or additional function to an item is simpler than creating something new. You don't need to invent a special formula or plan. Make a crafting roll to modify an item (the baseline quality of an item that you modify is equal to your crew's Tier, as usual).\n\n* A simple, useful modification requires Tier +1 quality. *A rifle that breaks down into two sections to be more easily concealed.*\n* A significant modification requires Tier +2 quality. *Strengthening the barrel and powder load of a gun to fire further.*\n* An arcane, spark-craft, or alchemical modification requires Tier +3 quality. *A dagger that can harm a demon. An electrified hull on a boat to repel boarders or ghosts. An outfit coated with chemicals to mask you from deathlands predators.*\n\nModified items, like special creations, may have **drawbacks**."
}
